4. Propulsion Topology: Double-Sided Halbach PMLSM

The selected propulsion topology is a double-sided, iron-core permanent-magnet linear synchronous motor with Halbach arrays. The Halbach configuration concentrates magnetic flux on the active side while reducing back-iron requirements, lowering mover mass and improving force ripple characteristics. The double-sided arrangement is essential for normal force cancellation.

The motor is segmented into shaft modules. Each module is defined as an opposing pair of stator sides. The module parameters are given in Table 5.

Parameter Value
Module length 2.0\ \text{m}
Nominal continuous thrust per module 6.5\ \text{kN}
Peak overload thrust per module 8.5\ \text{kN} for 10\ \text{s}
Active modules around capsule 4
Adjacent pre-excited modules 1
Available continuous thrust 26\ \text{kN}
Available peak thrust 34\ \text{kN}
Module controller Local SiC inverter and gate driver
Module sensing Current, temperature, DC bus voltage
Cooling Liquid-cooled serpentine plate

This configuration provides sufficient thrust margin for the required 25\ \text{kN} rated force while allowing one module to fail without immediate safety consequences. The N-1 criterion is satisfied: with four active modules, the failure of one leaves 19.5\ \text{kN} continuous thrust, sufficient for controlled deceleration at reduced acceleration.

