Appendix D. Normal Force Cancellation and Residual Budget Proof

D.1 Raw normal force

For iron-core PMLSM, the normal force is proportional to thrust:

F_{N,\text{raw}} = \kappa F_{em}, \quad \kappa \in [1.5, 3.0].

For F_{em} = 25\ \text{kN},

F_{N,\text{raw,min}} = 1.5 \times 25 = 37.5\ \text{kN},

F_{N,\text{raw,max}} = 3.0 \times 25 = 75.0\ \text{kN}.

D.2 Double-sided cancellation

In a double-sided arrangement, two stators act on opposite sides of the permanent-magnet secondary. The left stator produces normal force F_{N,L}, and the right stator produces F_{N,R}. Ideally,

F_{N,L} = -F_{N,R}.

The net normal force is

F_{N,\text{res}} = F_{N,L} + F_{N,R}.

D.3 Residual force budget

The residual arises from asymmetry in air gap, current, and magnetisation. The model is

F_{N,\text{res}} = k_g \Delta g + k_i \Delta i + k_m \Delta m,

where k_g, k_i, and k_m are sensitivity coefficients.

Preliminary values:

· air-gap stiffness k_g \approx 5.0\ \text{kN/mm};
· current imbalance sensitivity: \pm 2\% current asymmetry of 25\ \text{kN} thrust gives 1.1\ \text{kN};
· magnet tolerance \pm 3\% gives 1.1\ \text{kN}.

For \Delta g = 1\ \text{mm},

F_{N,\text{gap}} = 5.0 \times 1 = 5.0\ \text{kN}.

Thus, the worst-case residual is

F_{N,\text{res},\max} = 1.1 + 5.0 + 1.1 = 7.2\ \text{kN}.

The mechanical guide system is rated for

F_{N,\text{guide}} = 15.0\ \text{kN},

providing a safety factor of

S_{N} = \frac{15.0}{7.2} = 2.08.

The nominal residual target is below 4.0\ \text{kN}.

